<sn><md>| **Drainage Class**               | **Water Condition / Runoff**     | **Flooding Duration**   | **Soil Colour**    | **Grey Mottles / Redoximorphic Features**        |
| -------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |
| **Very Poorly Drained**          | Water remains for a long period  | 8–9 months/year         | Grey or dark grey  | Rarely present                                   |
| **Poorly Drained**               | Water remains for several months | Less than 8 months/year | Grey               | Brown mottles present                            |
| **Imperfectly Drained**          | Intermittently flooded           | Less than 15 days/year  | Grey or pale brown | Redoximorphic features (mottles) present         |
| **Moderately Well Drained**      | Non-flooded                      | No flooding             | Brown              | No grey mottles within **50 cm** of the surface  |
| **Well Drained**                 | Non-flooded                      | No flooding             | Brown              | No grey mottles within **100 cm** of the surface |
| **Somewhat Excessively Drained** | Water removed rapidly            | No flooding             | Brown or red       | No mottles throughout the soil profile           |
| **Excessively Drained**          | Water removed very rapidly       | No flooding             | Brown or red       | No grey mottles                                  |

**Note:** *Excessively drained* and *Somewhat excessively drained* soils are commonly found in **hilly areas**.
</md></sn>